B-box MITM certificate module

Namespace discovery and module packaging reference chen08209/FlClash dev,
commit 63aa150e23288558074d877f745a6d3b5f6418f6 (2026-11-01),
android/app/src/main/assets/mitm_ca and SystemCaStore.kt.
https://github.com/chen08209/FlClash/tree/63aa150e23288558074d877f745a6d3b5f6418f6/android/app/src/main/assets/mitm_ca

GPL-3.0. B-box changes (2026-11-03): export for manual installation by the
root manager; per-namespace staging before bind mounts; preserve each target's
CA set; no app-driven su/install/uninstall; only a public certificate included.
B-box changes (2026-11-05): inject Zygotes before enumerating all visible mount
namespaces; bounded fast boot retries followed by periodic reconciliation;
namespace/interpreter/script/certificate descriptors opened before nsenter;
namespace-local /dev staging; explicit pending/failure status and bounded logs.

Install this ZIP with Magisk, KernelSU or APatch, then reboot. Refresh the
certificate page in B-box to check this process's actual AndroidCAStore.
The service retries while booting, then checks every 30 seconds for new
namespaces and replaced CA mounts. mount.status describes the latest scan;
mount.log keeps up to 64 KiB of changed results. Root isolation policies may
prevent access, and existing app trust caches may require restarting the app.
System trust does not override app-specific trust stores or certificate pinning.
After regenerating the CA, update the module and reboot. Remove the module in
the root manager and reboot to remove its mounts. No private key is exported.
